s refused. Next: metais inspect <package>\n  manifest.* (44)       The manifest breaks one of its rules.\n                        Next: metais inspect <package>\n  markdown.* (3)        An input is refused. Next: metais inspect <package>\n  output.* (34)         An output fails its validation.\n                        Next: metais inspect <package>\n  output.* (14)         An output is refused. Next: metais inspect <package>\n  package.* (47)        The package is refused. Next: metais inspect <package>\n  schema.* (10)         An input schema is refused.\n                        Next: metais inspect <package>\n  schema.* (2)          With --sample, the generated data cannot be made or does\n                        not validate. Next: metais schema <package> <name>\n  template.* (23)       A template is refused. Next: metais inspect <package>\n  template.* (9)        An output's path, when or for_each does not parse.\n                        Next: metais inspect <package>\n  yaml.* (13)           An input is refused. Next: metais inspect <package>\n\nExamples:\n  metais render report-1.0.0.metais --data data --out out\n      Renders the package's outputs from the data directory data into the new\n      directory out.\n  metais render report.metais --data data --set /vendor/name=Acme --out out\n      Renders with one value set over the data directory's.\n  metais render . --data data --out out --now 2026-10-19T09:30:00+02:00 --json\n      Renders the source directory in the working directory with a render time,\n      and prints the files as one metais.render/1 document.\n  metais render report.metais --data data --out out --dry-run\n      Lists every file the render would write into out, with its size and\n      digest, and writes nothing.\n  metais render report.metais --data data --out - --only report.md\n      Renders the whole package and writes the bytes of report.md alone to\n      standard output.\n  metais render . --sample --out preview\n      Previews the 