or/name=Acme --out out\n      Renders with one value set over the data directory's.\n  metais render . --data data --out out --now 2026-10-19T09:30:00+02:00 --json\n      Renders the source directory in the working directory with a render time,\n      and prints the files as one metais.render/1 document.\n  metais render report.metais --data data --out out --dry-run\n      Lists every file the render would write into out, with its size and\n      digest, and writes nothing.\n  metais render report.metais --data data --out - --only report.md\n      Renders the whole package and writes the bytes of report.md alone to\n      standard output.\n  metais render . --sample --out preview\n      Previews the source directory's outputs from sample data.\n  metais render . --sample --set /incident/stage=final --seed 7 --out preview\n      Previews them with one value pinned and other generated values.\n  metais render report.metais --data data --out site --overwrite\n      Renders into the existing directory site, replacing the files the render\n      writes there and leaving every other one.\n----\nmetais validate — Validate inputs against a package, and report every finding at\nonce.\n\nUsage:\n  metais validate <package> [<supply flags>] [--resolved] [--json]\n\nOpens and verifies the package as inspect does, then assembles the inputs\nobject: each file of the data directory, then each --inputs-json in command-line\norder, then each --set and --set-json in command-line order, each replacing what\ncame before at its place. Each schema default is applied to a member left\nabsent, and the whole is validated against the package's schemas and its input\nconstraints.\n\nEvery finding is reported in one run: a file that does not parse does not stop\nthe others from being read and validated. With no supply flag, nothing is\nsupplied, and every required input is reported missing.\n\nThe result lists, for every input, whether it was supplied and where its value\ncame from. --resolved adds the inputs as templates would see them, after\ncoercion and defaults, in canonical key order; in human form it is printed as\nindented JSON after the findings.\n\nOperands:\n  <package>\n      A packed package file, or a source directory; - is refused, since a\n      package is read with random access. Required.\n\nFlags:\n  --data <dir>\n      The data directory: one file per input named <input>.<ext>, and one\n      directory per collection input. metais inspect lists each input's file\n      names.\n  --set <pointer>=<text>\n      Set one value at an inputs pointer, such as /vendor/name=Acme; the text is\n      coerced to the type the schema declares there. Applied after --data and\n      --inputs-json, in command-line order with --set-json. May be given more\n      than once.\n  --set-json <pointer>=<json>\n      Set one value at an inputs pointer as JSON text, the way to set null, an\n      array or an object. Applied in command-line order with --set. May be given\n----\nfile\t158\texamples/initial/example.yaml\ndir\t1\texamples/initial/expected/\nfile\t2073\texamples/initial/expected/incident-report.md\ndir\t3\texamples/initial/inputs/\nfile\t617\texamples/initial/inputs/entity.json\nfile\t831\texamples/initial/inputs/incident.json\nfile\t23\texamples/initial/inputs/stage.json\n\"initial notification\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01N9hBJZj8hR9K9QfHs2AUfz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
